{
  "slug": "artist:darkthrone",
  "name": "Darkthrone",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in 1986 as a death metal band named Black Death in Kolbotn, Norway, Darkthrone evolved into a fundamental force in the early Norwegian black metal scene by 1991. The duo, consisting of multi-instrumentalist Fenriz and vocalist Nocturno Culto, gained critical acclaim for their 'Unholy Trinity' of records: A Blaze in the Northern Sky (1992), Under a Funeral Moon (1993), and Transilvanian Hunger (1994). Their sound shifted dramatically in the 2000s, incorporating crust punk, speed metal, and traditional doom metal influences on albums like The Cult Is Alive and Eternal Hails......, reflecting an ongoing rejection of mainstream metal production standards. The band has famously opted out of live performances since 1996, focusing exclusively on studio output released through labels such as Peaceville and Moonfog Productions.",
